  When buttons are attached to a Slack tool-progress message, this rewrites the message as Block Kit with the visible text captured in the section block. Later progress updates still call `SlackAdapter.edit_message()`, which sends only top-level `text` and never rebuilds these blocks, so Slack clients can keep displaying this stale snapshot while the fallback text changes; update the Slack edit path to refresh the section and actions together while the message is an active busy-button anchor.

